nologically relevant. Pragmatically, our theory also enables significantly more efficient simulations that include noise at the droplet level [64]. In addition, we provide a foundation for more elaborate stochastic studies into shape fluctuations and droplet-droplet correlations, as well as for investigations into the large-activity and largenoise regimes.
